This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
## 1. Primary Request and Intent

This session covered building and iteratively refining a first-run onboarding wizard for the Workroom macOS app (GitHub issue #151: "New install setup — Need a great looking startup intro and flow for first time usage"), followed by a series of related UI polish requests. In chronological order, the user's explicit requests were:

1. Plan and review the onboarding wizard feature (via plan mode + `/plan-eng-review` skill)
2. Implement the approved plan
3. "leave this" (re: Window-menu suppression follow-up) / "tests should never use the real config" — two directives after I reported deviations from the plan
4. "run it" — launch the app to demo the feature
5. "only the onboarding wizard should open on a fresh start. Only open main window when the wizard is closed, or finished."
6. "run all the onboarding tests again" (repeated twice at different points)
7. "the nav dots on welcome screen shift when left and right buttons are added/removed. keep the dots centered so they don't shift"
8. "replace the 'sidebar' feature item with a version control item with a title of 'Version Control Built in'"
9. "add a 'Live activity + notifications' item."
10. "how does this all work for a branch new user? Can I try it?"
11. "rerun the UI tests" (multiple times)
12. "remove the title bar from welcome window"
13. Mid-turn: "in 'nothing selected' message, show workroom logo in place of generic terminal icon"
14. Mid-turn: "make it twice as big, and monochrome with no border" (re: the logo)
15. "the logo on that screen is bad quality" — required root-causing blurriness from upscaling a low-res source
16. "I've changed the 'nothing selected' text. Show relevant keyboard shortcuts in brackets next to open and create workroom text"
17. "close right sibar when no workroom is open" [sic] — most recent request, currently being verified

Throughout, the implicit standing intent was: every change must be verified via `make app-generate` → `make app-format` → `make app-build` → `make app-lint` (must stay clean) → relevant unit/UI tests → visual confirmation via screenshot/manual launch before considering it done. The user also cares about correctness at the root-cause level (rejected workarounds twice: once for the config-leak test issue, once implicitly by asking to rerun tests after the launch-behavior change, which surfaced a real regression).

## 2. Key Technical Concepts

- SwiftUI `Scene` composition: `WindowGroup(for:)`, `Window(_:id:)`, `.defaultLaunchBehavior(.presented/.suppressed/.automatic)`, `.windowResizability(.contentSize)`, `.windowStyle(.hiddenTitleBar)`
- `SceneBuilder` does NOT support `if/else` control flow between `Scene` values (confirmed by trying it — compile error), unlike `ViewBuilder`
- `Defaults` package (`sindresorhus/Defaults`) for persisted `UserDefaults`-backed keys — shared across all windows in the app, a key architectural constraint
- `WindowRegistry.shared.lastActiveStore` / `WindowRegistry.shared.register` — per-window `AppStore` coordination; deliberately NOT registering the onboarding window so it inherits Settings/About's aux-window treatment (⌘W fallback, shortcut/switcher no-ops, quit/window-count exclusion, ⌘` cycle exclusion)
- `UITestFixture` fixture-mode seam: `-WorkroomUITestFixture 1`, `-WorkroomUITestNoProjects 1`, deterministic fake projects, never touches real `~/.config/workroom/config.json` in fixture mode (this is the pattern the onboarding wizard's `addProject` fix needed to follow)
- `AppStore.bootstrap`/`load` already short-circuit to `loadFixture()` under `UITestFixture.isActive` — `addProject` was the one mutation that didn't follow this rule until fixed
- XCUITest automation subsystem "wedging" after repeated manual AppleScript/System Events driving — known environmental issue, not a code bug, requires login-session reset to clear
- `NSWindow.willCloseNotification` observer pattern for one-shot close handling
- Template image assets (`template-rendering-intent: template` in `Contents.json`) for monochrome, system-tinted icons
- `Scripts/make-icon.swift` — vector-based icon rendering (`renderMenuBarGlyph` draws `markBlocks` at any requested pixel size), run via `make app-icon`
- `ContentUnavailableView` with custom `Label { } icon: { }` and `description: { }` closures
- Go CLI `workroom` binary has no config-path override — a genuine architectural limitation that made test isolation tricky
- Codesigning breaks when `$HOME` is overridden (cert lookup needs real `~/Library/Keychains`)

## 3. Files and Code Sections

### `/Users/joelmoss/dev/workroom/macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/DefaultsKeys.swift`
- Added: `static let hasCompletedOnboarding = Key<Bool>("onboarding.hasCompleted", default: false)` with doc comment explaining it flips true on entering `.done` step by any path.

### `/Users/joelmoss/dev/workroom/macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/AppStore.swift`
- Changed `addProject(_ path: String, create: Bool) async` from returning `Void` to `Result<Void, Error>`, marked `@discardableResult`.
- Added fixture-mode short-circuit (root-cause fix per user's "tests should never use the real config" directive):
```swift
@discardableResult
func addProject(_ path: String, create: Bool) async -> Result<Void, Error> {
  // Fixture mode never shells out to the real CLI for anything else (`bootstrap`/`load` both
  // short-circuit to `loadFixture()`) — this is the one mutation that didn't follow that rule,
  // which meant a UI test driving the wizard's real Add Project step (issue #151) genuinely
  // registered a project in the developer's own `~/.config/workroom/config.json` (the CLI has no
  // config-path override to isolate against instead). Simulate the same success shape locally.
  if UITestFixture.isActive {
    let canonical = AddProjectSheetModel.normalize(path)
    if !projects.contains(where: { $0.path == canonical }) {
      projects.append(Project(path: canonical, vcs: "git", workrooms: []))
    }
    selectedProjectID = canonical
    selectedTargetID = .root(project: canonical)
    return .success(())
  }
  do {
    let canonical = try await cli.addProject(path, create: create)
    await reload()
    if let match = projects.first(where: { $0.path == canonical }) {
      selectedProjectID = match.id
      selectedTargetID = .root(project: match.path)
    }
    return .success(())
  } catch {
    present(error)
    return .failure(error)
  }
}
```

### `/Users/joelmoss/dev/workroom/macapp/WorkroomApp/Views/AddProjectSheet.swift`
- Extracted `AddProjectFields` view (the Picker + TextField + Choose button + footer caption), shared by `AddProjectSheet` and the new onboarding wizard's Add-Project step:
```swift
struct AddProjectFields: View {
  @Binding var mode: AddProjectMode
  @Binding var path: String
  @Binding var showChooser: Bool
  var pathFieldFocused: FocusState<Bool>.Binding
  var body: some View { /* Picker, TextField, Choose button, fileImporter */ }
}
```
- `AddProjectSheet` now wraps `AddProjectFields` in its own header/footer, behaviorally unchanged.

### `/Users/joelmoss/dev/workroom/macapp/WorkroomApp/Views/OnboardingWindow.swift` (new file)
- `enum OnboardingStep: Int, CaseIterable { case welcome, tour, addProject, done }`
- `enum OnboardingGate`:
```swift
enum OnboardingGate {
  static func shouldShow(
    hasCompleted: Bool, projectsEmpty: Bool, override: Bool? = UITestFixture.onboardingOverride
  ) -> Bool {
    if let override { return override }
    return !hasCompleted && projectsEmpty
  }

  /// A synchronous, pre-bootstrap approximation of `shouldShow` — `projectsEmpty` isn't known yet at
  /// the point the launch window decides whether to hide itself (that needs the async project-list
  /// load), so this is what drives that earlier decision instead.
  static func mightShow(hasCompleted: Bool, override: Bool? = UITestFixture.onboardingOverride)
    -> Bool
  {
    if let override { return override }
    return !hasCompleted
  }
}
```
- `OnboardingFeature` array — currently 5 items: workrooms, terminal, versionControl ("Version Control Built in" / `arrow.triangle.branch`), runCommand, activity ("Live activity + notifications" / `bell.badge`)
- `OnboardingWindow` struct: `.frame(width: 560, height: 480)`, `.windowStyle` set at the Scene level (see WorkroomApp.swift), form state (`addProjectMode`, `addProjectPath`, `showChooser`, `isAdding`, `addProjectError`) lifted to the parent so the footer can read validity
- `WindowAccessor` sets `window.isRestorable = false`, `window.setAccessibilityIdentifier("onboarding.window")` (fixes SwiftUI's `.accessibilityIdentifier` not reaching the NSWindow chrome), and a one-shot `NSWindow.willCloseNotification` observer that opens or fronts the main window:
```swift
var token: NSObjectProtocol?
token = NotificationCenter.default.addObserver(
  forName: NSWindow.willCloseNotification, object: window, queue: .main
) { [openWindow] _ in
  MainActor.assumeIsolated {
    if let hostWindow = WindowRegistry.shared.lastActiveStore?.hostWindow {
      hostWindow.makeKeyAndOrderFront(nil)
    } else {
      openWindow(value: WindowSeed.launch)
    }
  }
  if let token { NotificationCenter.default.removeObserver(token) }
}
```
- `.onChange(of: step)` sets `Defaults[.hasCompletedOnboarding] = true` on entering `.done` (fires regardless of how the window is later closed)
- `.task` correction logic (bootstraps a throwaway `AppStore` since the main window may be suppressed):
```swift
.task {
  guard ProcessInfo.processInfo.environment["XCTestConfigurationFilePath"] == nil else { return }
  guard OnboardingGate.mightShow(hasCompleted: Defaults[.hasCompletedOnboarding]) else { return }
  let probe = AppStore(projectStore: .shared)
  await probe.bootstrap(restore: false)
  if !OnboardingGate.shouldShow(
    hasCompleted: Defaults[.hasCompletedOnboarding], projectsEmpty: probe.projects.isEmpty
  ) {
    openWindow(value: WindowSeed.launch)
    dismissWindow(id: Self.sceneID)
  }
}
```
- `footer` uses `.overlay(alignment: .center) { stepDots }` instead of a double-`Spacer()` sandwich, to keep the dots visually centered regardless of asymmetric button groups per step (fix for the "nav dots shift" bug report).
- `handleAdd()` falls back to a throwaway store when no window is registered yet:
```swift
private func handleAdd() async {
  isAdding = true
  defer { isAdding = false }
  // No launch window may exist yet at all now (issue #151: the main `WindowGroup` is
  // launch-suppressed while onboarding might be needed)... Falling back to a throwaway store
  // still correctly registers the project (it mutates the same shared `ProjectStore.shared`)...
  let store = WindowRegistry.shared.lastActiveStore ?? AppStore(projectStore: .shared)
  let normalized = AddProjectSheetModel.normalize(addProjectPath)
  switch await store.addProject(normalized, create: addProjectMode == .createNew) {
  case .success:
    addProjectError = nil
    step = .done
  case .failure(let error):
    addProjectError = (error as? LocalizedError)?.errorDescription ?? error.localizedDescription
  }
}
```
- `OnboardingTourStep` wraps the feature-card list in a `ScrollView` (fix for overflow risk after adding the 5th card).

### `/Users/joelmoss/dev/workroom/macapp/WorkroomApp/WorkroomApp.swift`
- `var body: some Scene` now computes `let onboardingMightShow = OnboardingGate.mightShow(hasCompleted: Defaults[.hasCompletedOnboarding])` once, then applies:
```swift
WindowGroup(for: WindowSeed.self) { ... }
  .commands { WorkroomCommands(updater: updater) }
  .defaultLaunchBehavior(onboardingMightShow ? .suppressed : .automatic)

Settings { ... }

Window("Welcome to Workroom", id: OnboardingWindow.sceneID) { OnboardingWindow() }
  .windowResizability(.contentSize)
  .windowStyle(.hiddenTitleBar)
  .defaultLaunchBehavior(onboardingMightShow ? .presented : .suppressed)
```
- Removed the earlier (broken) `window.orderOut(nil)` hack from `RootWindow`'s `WindowAccessor` and the corresponding `.task` logic that called `openWindow(id: OnboardingWindow.sceneID)` — this whole approach was replaced by `.defaultLaunchBehavior`.
- Removed the now-unused `RootWindow.shouldOpenOnboarding` static helper (and its tests, see below) since the gating moved to the Scene-level `.defaultLaunchBehavior` + `OnboardingWindow`'s own correction task.
- `RootWindow`'s `.task` is now back to its original simple form (just `bootstrap` + session-restore fan-out), no onboarding logic left in it.

### `/Users/joelmoss/dev/workroom/macapp/WorkroomApp/Core/UITestFixture.swift`
- Added `onboardingOverride: Bool?` (reads `-WorkroomUITestOnboarding show|hide`)
- Added `onboardingRealGate: Bool` (reads `-WorkroomUITestOnboardingRealGate 1`) — stops `applyFixtureDefaults` from pinning `hasCompletedOnboarding = true`
- Added `onboardingSeed: Bool?` (reads `-WorkroomUITestOnboardingSeed true|false`) — explicit seed value written from inside the app itself (needed because an external `defaults write` from the test process empirically didn't reliably reach the freshly-launched app's own `UserDefaults` read — a cross-process cfprefsd quirk specific to the xcodebuild-test launch path)
- In `applyFixtureDefaults`:
```swift
if let seed = onboardingSeed {
  Defaults[.hasCompletedOnboarding] = seed
} else if !onboardingRealGate {
